/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105391","id":2806829886,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nTNM-","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T16:46:38Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T16:46:38Z","body":"I see you've been force-pushing a lot 😅 \r\n\r\nAre the CI tests giving you trouble? If so, you may be able to check what commands they're running and execute them locally to get quicker feedback. If all else fails, I think you can create a new testing branch on your fork and push your changes to there so you can use the GitHub CI services without it updating the PR thread. Then, once everything looks good, you can update the PR branch.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2806829886/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2806996597","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105391#issuecomment-2806996597","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105391","id":2806996597,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nT151","user":{"login":"Raftatul","id":80292778,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMjkyNzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80292778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul","html_url":"https://github.com/Raftatul","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T17:41:33Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T17:41:33Z","body":"> I see you've been force-pushing a lot 😅\r\n> \r\n> Are the CI tests giving you trouble? If so, you may be able to check what commands they're running and execute them locally to get quicker feedback. If all else fails, I think you can create a new testing branch on your fork and push your changes to there so you can use the GitHub CI services without it updating the PR thread. Then, once everything looks good, you can update the PR branch.\r\n\r\nI finally managed to pass the check ! And yeah I force-pushed to keep a single commit in the PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2806996597/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2813248383","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105391#issuecomment-2813248383","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105391","id":2813248383,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nrsN_","user":{"login":"btarg","id":27726289,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NzI2Mjg5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27726289?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/btarg","html_url":"https://github.com/btarg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btarg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btarg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btarg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btarg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btarg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btarg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btarg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btarg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btarg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-17T15:04:46Z","updated_at":"2025-04-17T15:04:46Z","body":"I use curves a lot for animating/tweening via lerp, this would be an incredible QoL improvement! Thank you!","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2813248383/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888514926","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105391#issuecomment-2888514926","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105391","id":2888514926,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sKz1u","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T17:57:25Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T17:57:25Z","body":"The implementation seems fine, but I don't really see much benefit. `set_custom_interpolator()` can achieve the same effect for PropertyTweener, and for MethodTweener the curve can be part of your method. The only advantage of `set_curve()` is that you can set the curve to apply for the whole Tween. Is it really common though to tween multiple properties with the same curve? \r\n\r\nMy main problem with the new method is that it adds another way to do the same thing. It's arguably easier to use, but makes Tween more complex and just not sure if it's worth it.\r\n\r\nI compared 3 different ways of interpolating a curve:\r\n```GDScript\r\ntween.tween_property(self, \"position\", Vector2(600, 550), 2.0).from(Vector2(150, 550)).set_curve(curve)\r\ntween.tween_property(self, \"position\", Vector2(600, 550), 2.0).from(Vector2(150, 550)).set_custom_interpolator(tween_curve)\r\ntween.tween_method(tween_curve2.bind(Vector2(150, 550), Vector2(600, 550)), 0.0, 1.0, 2.0)\r\n```\r\nWhere\r\n```GDScript\r\nfunc tween_curve2(v, from, to):\r\n\treturn lerp(from, to, curve.sample_baked(v))\r\n\r\nfunc tween_curve(v):\r\n\treturn curve.sample_baked(v)\r\n```\r\n(you can make these methods globally available, they are universal)\r\n\r\n`tween_method()` actually turns out the shortest, if you don't count the helper method which can be reused.\r\n\r\nIf setting the curve for the whole Tween is the deal breaker here, maybe the custom interpolator can be extended (also adding it to MethodTweener would allow having single helper method).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888514926/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888542455","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105391#issuecomment-2888542455","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105391","id":2888542455,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sK6j3","user":{"login":"avedar","id":70921399,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTIxMzk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70921399?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar","html_url":"https://github.com/avedar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T19:08:46Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T19:08:46Z","body":"Tweens are always shown and explained as properties following a curve so I feel like it's a very clear and obvious expectation to be able to set your own curves. Even though it's not particularly difficult, I don't think tweening methods is obvious at all and definitely not the first thing that comes to mind when you're already expecting the Tween class to do the work for you.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888542455/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888545532","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105391#issuecomment-2888545532","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105391","id":2888545532,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sK7T8","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T19:17:22Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T19:17:22Z","body":"We can add ready-to-copy-paste code samples to the documentation. From discoverability standpoint, the only problem right now is that searching for \"curve\" in Tween doc page yields no results.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888545532/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888557537","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105391#issuecomment-2888557537","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105391","id":2888557537,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sK-Ph","user":{"login":"avedar","id":70921399,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTIxMzk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70921399?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar","html_url":"https://github.com/avedar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avedar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T19:48:34Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T19:48:34Z","body":"I wouldn't be against adding more examples of method tweening. However, despite lack of direct references to curves, the documentation points to [this image](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot-docs/master/img/tween_cheatsheet.webp) which I feel is a pretty universal depiction of what tweens are doing and evokes ideas of customization. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888557537/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888588958","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105391#issuecomment-2888588958","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105391","id":2888588958,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sLF6e","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T21:21:10Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T21:52:32Z","body":"Since it is a fairly common concept that tweening is done with some built-in formulas, I think not having optional curves in there is to be expected. Like [cocos2d](https://docs.cocos.com/creator/3.4/manual/en/tween/tween-function.html), [tween.js](https://sole.github.io/tween.js/examples/03_graphs.html).\r\n\r\nIf I improve the documentation, I would include an example that curves can be created as a resource and used with the tween's `set_custom_interpolator()`, as in “If you want to use arbitrary curves, you can do so as follows”.\r\n\r\nSo at least as described in @KoBeWi , `set_curve()` could be written more simply as a syntax sugar for custom interpolator in C++ code. However, I cannot judge whether `set_curve()` method has more worth than documenting custom interpolator; It may be sufficient to distribute a script that collects several `set_custom_interpolator()` syntax sugars as a static method in the asset store as an addon.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888588958/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888601879","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105391#issuecomment-2888601879","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105391","id":2888601879,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sLJEX","user":{"login":"Raftatul","id":80292778,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMjkyNzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80292778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul","html_url":"https://github.com/Raftatul","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Raftatul/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T21:59:18Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T21:59:18Z","body":"This PR was about allowing curves to be used out of the box. But if the documentation is updated to mention curves and includes codes to achieve the same result, then I think that’s ok. However, note that this PR overrides the tween's easing and transition, which I believe is a good UX improvement, the curve the user sees is the actual curve applied to the tween.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888601879/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888603390","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105391#issuecomment-2888603390","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105391","id":2888603390,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sLJb-","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T22:03:52Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T22:03:52Z","body":"> this PR overrides the tween's easing and transition, which I believe is a good UX improvement, the curve the user sees is the actual curve applied to the tween.\r\n\r\nThe default transition is linear, so unless you change it, it's the same with custom interpolator.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888603390/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]